{"files":[{"content":"#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <string.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n\n    int i, j, x;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        for (j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n\n            /* A full list cannot accept a distance at or beyond its maximum. */\n            if (k > 0 && distances[k - 1] != -1.0f &&\n                d >= distances[k - 1]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            /* Find the first matching slot using independent comparisons. */\n            int insertion = k;\n            #pragma omp simd reduction(min:insertion)\n            for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                float stored = distances[x];\n                int candidate = (d < stored || stored == -1.0f) ? x : k;\n                insertion = candidate < insertion ? candidate : insertion;\n            }\n\n            if (insertion < k) {\n                size_t tail = (size_t) (k - insertion - 1);\n                if (tail != 0) {\n                    memmove(distances + insertion + 1,\n                            distances + insertion,\n                            tail * sizeof(*distances));\n                    memmove(labels + insertion + 1,\n                            labels + insertion,\n                            tail * sizeof(*labels));\n                }\n\n                distances[insertion] = d;\n                labels[insertion] = g.label;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(distances);\n    free(labels);\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n","path":"src/knn.c"}],"hypothesis":"A SIMD minimum-index reduction can replace the branch-dependent insertion search, while a full-list cutoff avoids unnecessary searches on ARM64.","notes":"Not executed. Scalar distance arithmetic, traversal order, sentinel handling, and stable neighbor ties are retained. Updates remain serial; overlapping shifts use memmove.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace the early-exit slot search with independent predicates and an OpenMP SIMD integer minimum reduction.","Reject distances greater than or equal to the final retained distance when the list is full.","Replace dependent backward shifts with overlap-safe memmove calls.","Release per-call selection buffers before returning."]}